<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Japanese. English in res/values is the fallback for anything missing here.

    Japanese is dense rather than long, so these are shorter than the German and
    French files and the fixed-height controls are comfortable. Two things to
    watch when editing:

      * No kanji-only shorthand for the player-facing rules. The how-to-play
        lines are read by a player who has never seen the game, so they are
        written in plain form rather than telegraphed game shorthand.
      * Full-width punctuation (、 。！) reads correctly here; do not swap it for
        the ASCII forms used in the English file.

    Rendering note: Poppins carries no CJK glyphs. See
    ui/theme/LocalizedType.kt - the bundled family is used when it covers the
    script and the system CJK family takes over when it does not, so these
    strings never fall back to tofu boxes.
-->
